{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310850,"nonce":"531NMD01NvqgFZWKhU1yZOleNlI=","title":"@:move + @:derive(Clone) are now runtime-load-bearing end-to-end. Six interlocking fixes — Cranelift entry-block liveness seed, ...","message":"`@:move` and `@:derive([Clone])` are now wired end-to-end on `rayzor.ds.Tensor` and `rayzor.ds.QTensor` as of commits b3d9968 + d2e6d27 + fab97bc + 49cb959. Two workflows: wkrmf71el surfaced 6 RED blockers via adversarial verify; wlxn3joln fix-forward landed all six, all three reviewers (correctness / regression / semantics) refused to refute.\n\n**Why:** the prior project memo `project_ownership_no_enforcement` documented that E0382 was a soft warning and `@:move` was metadata-only. Without runtime enforcement, the pool allocator + addInto fused-kernel work could not assume disjoint buffers — every \"optimisation\" implicitly trusted Haxe's GC-style aliasing. Strict move makes downstream alias-aware optimisations safe.\n\n**How to apply:** when proposing pool allocator, addInto fused kernel, or any other in-place / borrow / move-aware optimisation, you can now treat `@:move`-annotated classes as Rust-grade. User-side `var b = a;` after a consume is E0300 hard-error at compile time and CheckLive trap on the JIT-native path. The runtime `rayzor_tensor_clone` / `rayzor_qtensor_clone` produce genuinely disjoint buffers (no view passthrough).\n\n\n1. **Cranelift entry-block liveness seed** — `collect_liveness_ids` pre-walks every block in `func.cfg.blocks`, gathers every IrId used by `MarkMoved` / `CheckLive`, allocates 1-byte `ExplicitSlot`s, and emits `iconst I8=1 + stack_store` into entry_block while the builder is still positioned there, before block_map / per-block RPO translation begins. Lazy first-encounter seeding was unsound — `ExplicitSlot` starts undefined per Cranelift docs, so CFG paths bypassing the seed read garbage. `get_or_alloc_liveness_slot` is now a pure lookup that panics if asked for an unseeded IrId. See `cranelift_backend.rs:1665-1675` + `2167-2180`.\n\n2. **Per-function state clearing** — `strict_move_locals.clear()` at all 10 function-body entry/exit sites in `hir_to_mir.rs` paired with `symbol_map.clear`, plus snapshot+restore in 5 thunk / constructor-reflect-wrapper / `__vtable_init__` / `__init__` paths and via `SavedLoweringState` for nested lambda/async lowering. `moved_ids` in `mir_interpreter.rs:1199-1211` uses `std::mem::take` before `stack.push` and explicit restore after `stack.pop` on BOTH Ok and Err paths (exec_result bound before `?`). IrId numbering restarts per function — without clears, unrelated registers inherit move-state.\n\n3. **Unconditional deep-copy clones** — `rayzor_tensor_clone` and `rayzor_qtensor_clone` no longer pass-through views. Both allocate fresh wrapper + shape + strides + data with `owns_data=true`. Tensor view extent: `(Σ(shape[i]-1)·strides[i] + 1)·elem_size` (covers every reachable element under the strided pattern). QTensor uses scheme-derived block bytes: INT8=numel, Q4_K_M=(numel/256)·144, Q6_K=(numel/256)·210.\n\n4. **Tier B FQN routing** — extern `@:derive(Clone)` reads class-level `@:native(\"...\")` metadata, normalises `::` → `.`, and only matches the exact strings `\"rayzor.ds.Tensor\"` / `\"rayzor.ds.QTensor\"`. User extern classes named Tensor/QTensor in other packages fall through to Tier A field-by-field. `hir_to_mir.rs:35639-35663`.\n\n5. **TraitChecker cross-file merge** — `TraitChecker.extend_classes(\u0026[TypedClass]) -\u003e Self` builder method or_inserts (existing entries win) every loaded stdlib file's classes after the user file. Cross-file `@:move` on stdlib types was previously invisible to `requires_strict_move` at user-call sites. `compilation.rs:5867-5875`. Adds opt-in `RAYZOR_DEBUG_E0382` env var that dumps var/symbol/file/severity/move-and-use sites before each E0382 (renderer falls back to `user_files[0]` for cross-file modules — the dump is the only triangulation tool).\n\n6. **DataId-per-name interning** — `liveness_names` map populated from `function.locals` and `function.signature.parameters` with `\u003canon\u003e` fallback. `string_data: BTreeMap\u003cString, DataId\u003e` is content-keyed by variable name, not by IrId, so growth is bounded by distinct-variable-count not CheckLive-site-count.\n\n\n- 709 compiler-lib + 88 runtime-lib + 128/128 haxe regression PASS\n- tiny-transformer === PASS === deterministic across two runs\n- llama-chat `compare.sh \"What is the capital of France?\" 12` returns **MATCH: outputs are identical** vs llama.cpp Metal byte-for-byte\n- bench: 3 runs avg ~14.38 s / 0.853 tok/s vs ~14.7 s / 0.84 tok/s baseline (~2% faster, within noise)\n- nue/* call sites fixed: GQAttention (q/k/scores chain), MultiHeadAttention (triple Q/K/V), SwiGLU (gate clone), TransformerBlock (pre-norm residual), Linear (qweight branch), LlamaModel.forwardIds (per-iter hIn rebind), BertModel.encode (hN chain)\n\n\n- [[bugs-clone-view-passthrough-invariant]] — cloned views have `owns_data=true` but non-contiguous strides; no kernel reads this as a contiguity flag today, but watch any future fast-path memcpy\n- [[bugs-cranelift-liveness-dead-params]] — dead `_builder`/`_entry_block` params on `get_or_alloc_liveness_slot`\n- [[bugs-c-backend-move-noop]] — c_backend silently no-ops MarkMoved/CheckLive; needs layering doc-comment\n\n\n- Initial workflow (RED): `wkrmf71el` — 16 agents, found 6 blockers\n- Fix-forward (GREEN): `wlxn3joln` — 11 agents, all blockers resolved, three-perspective adversarial verify all refused to refute\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_move_clone_enforced` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}